      "rationale": "L1\u2013L4 all report the same CD36-V5\u00d77-GFP construct in which seven V5 tags are distributed across the extracellular domain (residues 31\u2013439) and are accessible to anti-V5 antibody from the extracellular face without permeabilization, establishing that the ectodomain tolerates short epitope-tag insertions. No individual residue junction is named in any of the four clips, so insert_after_residue is left null and the site is classified at region level. The position_evidence is 'inferred' because the exact junctions were not disclosed; the cited_tag_residue is null for the same reason. This is the strongest extracellular-surface evidence in the ledger for CD36. Full-length CD36 with seven V5 epitope tag sequences inserted into the extracellular domain (residues 31\u2013439) and GFP fused to the intracellular C-terminus, expressed in mammalian cells (CD36-V5\u00d77-GFP reporter). Anti-V5 immunofluorescence without cell permeabilization confirmed that the V5 tags are surface-displayed when the reporter reaches the plasma membrane.",
